    "narrative": "Our strongest play heading into today\u2019s slate is **James Wood** (73.98), who benefits from a prime matchup against the 4.71 xERA of G. Holmes. With an elite xwOBA of 0.423 and the advantage of leading off, **James Wood** is our anchor for both R and SB production. We are also leaning heavily on **Josh Naylor** (65.47) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (64.03); while **Josh Naylor** faces a difficult assignment against Roki Sasaki, his current form and the favorable wind conditions at the park provide a solid floor. **Tyler Soderstrom** receives a significant boost from park factors, helping him overcome a respectable matchup against Sonny Gray to remain a high-upside play in the middle of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench centered on **Seiya Suzuki** (59.74), who just narrowly missed the 60-point threshold required for a \"Strong\" recommendation. While he benefits from hitting second and facing a slower-delivery pitcher which may assist in stealing a bag, his negative park factor ultimately pushed his efficiency score slightly below the starting cut-off compared to the superior park-adjusted profiles of **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Josh Naylor**. **Dalton Rushing** (44.69) and **Cole Young** (52.73) remain our most speculative starts, as both are subject to the \"Lineup Pending\" tag. Should **Dalton Rushing** drop further down in the order than the projected #9 spot, his efficiency score will likely plummet, and we may look to preserve our game caps by pulling him from the lineup entirely. We continue to monitor the status of **Brice Turang**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** for potential spot-start opportunities later this week, while **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Trevor Story** remain unavailable for today's action due to off-days, rest, or injury.",
